          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesViaHigherGeometry"} Via higher geometry
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em T-fold
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hull04"}> Hull 04
            ) is supposed to be a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            that locally has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifolds"} Riemannian manifolds
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            (i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe+with+connection"} bundle gerbe with connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            (as an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            is) but also by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            transformations along some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
          %p
            The idea is that a T-fold is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            that is only locally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            but globally a more general kind of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-geometric+backgrounds"} non-geometric backgrounds
            is used for such “generalized geometric” backgrounds.
          %p
            It is expected that T-folds should have a description in terms of spaces that locally are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            of one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            with its T-dual, as the correspondence spaces considered in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} infinitesimal
            approximation this is derived from analysis of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} super p-brane WZ-terms
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FSS16"} FSS 16
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality+2-group"} T-duality 2-group
            is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#NikolausWaldorf18"} Nikolaus-Waldorf 18
          %p
            One may then consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local field theory
            on these double torus fibrations, and this should be closely related to what is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"} double field theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hull06"}> Hull 06
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+geometry"} type II geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-geometric+string+theory+vacua"} non-geometric string theory vacua
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doubled+geometry"}> doubled geometry
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+geometry"} type II geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"} double field theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original idea:
          %ul
            %li#Hull04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Geometry for Non-Geometric String Backgrounds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0406102"} arXiv:hep-th/0406102
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"} double field theory
            goes back to:
          %ul
            %li#Hull06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
              ,
              %em Doubled geometry and T-folds
              JHEP0707:080,2007 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605149"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605149
              )
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                %em Global Aspects of T-Duality, Gauged Sigma Models and T-Folds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0604178"}> arXiv:hep-th/0604178
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Bergman"}> Aaron Bergman
                , Daniel Robbins,
                %em Ramond-Ramond Fields, Cohomology and Non-Geometric Fluxes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0710.5158"}> arXiv:0710.5158
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"}> Dieter Lüst
                , Stefano Massai, Valentí Vall Camell,
                %em The monodromy of T-folds and T-fects
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.01193"}> arXiv:1508.01193
                )
            %li
              %p
                Yoan Gautier,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"} Chris Hull
                %em Heterotic/type II Duality and Non-Geometric Compactifications
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.02165"}> arXiv:1906.02165
                )
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+T-duality"} nonabelian T-duality
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Mark Bugden,
                %em Non-abelian T-folds
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.03782"}> arXiv:1901.03782
                )
            %li
              %p
                Ladislav Hlavatý, Ivo Petr,
                %em T-folds as Poisson-Lie plurals
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.08387"}> arXiv:2004.08387
                )
          %p
            Comments in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bouwknegt"}> Peter Bouwknegt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashwin+S.+Pande"} Ashwin S. Pande
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological T-duality and T-folds
              %strong 13
              5 (2009) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4374"}> arXiv:0810.4374
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2009.v13.n5.a6"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2009.v13.n5.a6
          %h3#ReferencesViaHigherGeometry Via higher geometry
          %p
            A global definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-folds"} T-folds
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            understood as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+T-duality"} topological T-duality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundles"} principal 2-bundles
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality+2-group"} T-duality 2-group
            (as described in
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-Duality+and+Differential+K-Theory"} T-Duality and Differential K-Theory
          %ul
            %li#Nikolaus14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em T-Duality in K-theory and elliptic cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Geometry Network Meeting
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ingvet.kau.se/juerfuch/conf/esi14/esi14_34.html"} website
            %li#NikolausWaldorf18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher geometry for non-geometric T-duals
                %strong 374
                (2020) 317-366 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.00677"}> arXiv:1804.00677
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03496-3"} doi:10.1007/s00220-019-03496-3
          %p
            The local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            of T-folds compatible with this proposal is derived from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"}
              fundamental super
              = succeed "-brane" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            in:
          %ul
            %li#FSS16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/T-Duality+from+super+Lie+n-algebra+cocycles+for+super+p-branes"} T-Duality from super Lie n-algebra cocycles for super p-branes
              %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/pages/journals/items/atmp/content/vols/0022/0005/"} ATMP Volume 22 (2018) Number 5
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.06536"}> arXiv:1611.06536
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2018.v22.n5.a3"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2018.v22.n5.a3
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality+2-group"} T-duality 2-group
            (and hence potentially the full structure of T-folds) is determined in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
              ,
              %em Categorical symmetries of T-duality
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.09187"}> arXiv:2202.09187
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/2035224"} spire:2035224
          %p Introduction and review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stacks, Gerbes and T-Duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/waldorf19notes.pdf", :title => "Waldorf (2019) notes"} Waldorf (2019) notes
          %p
            Proposals for further generalization (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+2-bundle"} 2-connections
            and further
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-geometric+backgrounds"} non-geometric backgrounds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hyungrok+Kim"}> Hyungrok Kim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"} Christian Saemann
              %em Non-Geometric T-Duality as Higher Groupoid Bundles with Connections
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.01783"}> arXiv:2204.01783
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
